          <p>Then you skip the grid and use the form. The list above is the set of states we have written a page for, not the set we fly to. A bird bound for Montana costs the same to send as one bound for Michigan, and the paperwork is identical.</p>

          <h5>We Ship to All Fifty States From Midland, Texas</h5>
          <p>Airline live-animal cargo reaches every state in the country, and so do we. The only thing a missing tile changes is that you tell us your city in a sentence instead of clicking it.</p>

          <h6>From Midland: How We Decide the Route</h6>
          <p>Flight time first, then handling. A direct flight to a bigger airport two hours from you beats a connection into the airport across town, because every connection is another hour on a warm ramp. We book the shortest day for the bird and tell you where that lands.</p>
