          </div>
          <p class="cap">Where a state page does not yet name a cargo counter we say so rather than guess; we confirm the airport when you tell us your city.</p>

          <h3>Pickup in Midland, Texas — Within Two or Three Hours</h3>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "midland-pickup-within-two-or-three-hours-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "midland-pickup-within-two-or-three-hours-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "midland-pickup-within-two-or-three-hours-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="The drive-time band inside which buyers collect in person">
          <p>Collecting in person costs nothing and it is the way we would buy a bird ourselves. You meet the parents, you see the room the chick was weaned in, and the bird rides home in your car in a carrier on the passenger seat. Buyers inside that radius collect in person, and the drive home with the carrier belted in is the first hour of the bird's new life with you.</p>

          <h3>Everywhere Else Flies</h3>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "everywhere-else-flies-nationwide-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "everywhere-else-flies-nationwide-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "everywhere-else-flies-nationwide-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Flight arcs fanning out to buyers beyond the drive radius">
          <p>Past the drive line the bird flies as manifested live-animal cargo on the shortest route we can book. <a href="https://www.iata.org/en/programs/ops-infra/live-animals/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The IATA Live Animals Regulations ↗</a> set the crate standard, and the crate is built to them. Delta Cargo, United Cargo and American Airlines Cargo all carry them; which one we use depends on your city. Total transit is usually under eight hours, and the bird is fully weaned and vet-cleared before it is booked, never the other way round.</p>
          <p class="ship-line">Ships nationwide · <b>{airport}</b> airport cargo · <b>{home}</b> home delivery · a cabin seat with a flight nanny is quoted per route, {cabin} · collection here is free within a two to three hour drive.</p>

          <h4>How Much Is Delivery to Your Address?</h4>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "how-much-delivery-to-your-address-costs-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "how-much-delivery-to-your-address-costs-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "how-much-delivery-to-your-address-costs-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Airport collection set against door delivery by what each costs">
          <p>{home}, flat, anywhere in the country, on a date we agree with you first. It is the airport route plus the last leg to your door, and it suits buyers who cannot get to a cargo desk on a weekday afternoon. Most people choose the airport and save the difference; a pair of birds and anyone more than an hour from the counter are the two cases where we suggest the door.</p>

          <h5>{airport} to Your Nearest Cargo Airport, {home} to Your Door</h5>
          <p>Two numbers, printed here and on every bird card, and the same in Maine as in Arizona. There is no surcharge for a “remote” state and no fee added after you reserve. If you ever see a delivery figure from us that is not one of those two, it is a cabin seat, and we will have said so in writing.</p>

          <h6>From Midland: The Drive-or-Fly Line</h6>
          <p>Roughly three hours by car in any direction. Inside it, come and get your bird. Outside it, we do not drive, because a bird in a car for nine hours has had a worse day than a bird in a crate for four. The flight is kinder, and it is what we would choose for our own.</p>
